    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-111",
      "nuance_tags": ["humility", "politeness"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "business", "formal-email"],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix: the honorific prefix お/ご sits in front of the base and no op in the enum places material ahead of it, so no step list reaches the surface. The suffixal half is masu-stem + する (持つ -> 持ち -> お持ちする), but the choice between お and ご is lexical — お for native 和語 verbs, ご for Sino-Japanese 漢語 compounds, with memorized exceptions — and cannot be derived from the base token.",
      "variants": []
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-112",
      "nuance_tags": ["humility", "politeness"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "business", "formal-email"],
      "steps_unavailable": "いたす is a suppletive lexical replacement for する, not a derivation from a base: no op in the enum produces it. The productive half the record gives (Sino-Japanese verbal noun + いたす, 説明する -> 説明いたします) requires a サ変 verbal-noun base that the base enum cannot express; declaring base \"noun\" would license *学生いたします.",
